<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} image="/assets/situations/darvo-blame-reversal.webp" bodyClass="editorial-page pillar-guide-page" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="answer-page pillar-guide">
    <header class="page-header shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Pillar guide</p>
      <h1>DARVO Response: Stop the Role Reversal</h1>
      <div class="answer-lead">
        <p>{description}</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="shell-narrow article-body" set:html={contentHtml.replace(
      "<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>",
      `<h2>The smallest usable version</h2>
<p>If you freeze, do not try to explain the whole pattern. Use one sentence that refuses the role reversal and returns to the issue.</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“I’m not calling you the bad guy. I’m talking about what happened.”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“I’m not calling you the bad guy. I’m talking about what happened.”">Copy</button></div>
<p>If they keep making their hurt the only topic, add:</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“We can talk about your reaction after we finish the original issue.”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“We can talk about your reaction after we finish the original issue.”">Copy</button></div>
<p>If they still reverse it, stop trying to win the frame:</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“This has flipped away from the issue. I’m going to pause here.”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“This has flipped away from the issue. I’m going to pause here.”">Copy</button></div>
